description = "An emulator of the Apple II+ and the Apple //e, written in Go. The ROMs and a DOS 3.3 diskette are built into the core, so it starts into Applesoft BASIC with no content loaded. It boots 5 1/4 diskettes in DSK, PO, NIB and WOZ format, 3.5 disks and hard disks in 2MG and HDV format, and reads cassette tapes from WAV recordings, compressed with gzip or zip or not. Games spanning several diskettes are loaded from an M3U playlist and swapped from the disk control menu. The default machine is an enhanced Apple //e with a Mockingboard, set up for playing games."

notes = "The core has no savestates, so rewind, run ahead and netplay are not available.|Super hi-res, the Videx 80 column video and the RGB card modes are not rendered, so the box art of collections like Total Replay is not shown. The 80 columns of the Apple //e do work, they are a mode of the machine and not a card.|For a game on several diskettes, load an M3U playlist listing them, one path per line.|Games save into an overlay file in the save directory, holding only the parts written. The disk image loaded is never modified, diskettes and hard disks alike, so compressed and read only disks can be saved to as well.|WOZ and NIB diskettes cannot save.|The gaps between the scan lines are not drawn, use a shader for the CRT look. The monitor, NTSC colour or green phosphor, is a core option.|Disk access runs faster than the real machine, and the sound breaks up while it does."
